<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ApprovalProcess xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <ApprovalProcess> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error. The rationale below lives in this comment
        rather than in <description> because a comment is repo-only and is never sent to the
        Metadata API. ⚠ DO NOT ASSUME THE 255-CHARACTER CAP that binds RecordType and
        ValidationRule descriptions applies here: the five approval files already in this repo
        carry descriptions of 442 to 617 characters (measured against git HEAD, 2026-08-19).
        The descriptions written in this change are nevertheless kept under 255, so the rule is
        uniform across every metadata type in this tranche and never has to be re-measured.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 REPOINTED 2026-08-19. THIS PROCESS CHANGED OBJECT-ROLE, NOT JUST CRITERIA.
        =====================================================================================
        It used to approve the listing broker chosen from BOV responses, on the ON-MARKET path,
        at BOV Outreach. That job moved to a NEW approval on a DIFFERENT OBJECT:
        approvalProcesses/BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Finalize_Approval, which approves the
        SELECTED SUBMISSION rather than the Disposition. This process now covers the OFF-MARKET
        path only, where there is no BOV beauty parade and the broker is a direct pick.

        🔴 THE SELF-LIMITING RATIONALE IS DEAD. Quoted and retracted rather than deleted,
        because it is an explicit instruction NOT to add the criterion this file now carries:

            RETRACTED: "Entry: the disposition is at BOV Outreach. This is self-limiting to the
            On Market path because BOV Outreach exists only in the On_Market value set - no
            RecordType criterion is needed and none should be added. No field updates fire on
            approval or rejection."

        WHY IT DIED: 'Broker Selection' is on BOTH record types' value sets (the redesign put it
        there), so the new entry stage is NOT self-limiting the way BOV Outreach was. A record-
        type criterion is now REQUIRED, and without it an on-market disposition sitting at
        Broker Selection would enter this process and be advanced straight to NDA, skipping the
        manual Advance to NDA hop that the on-market path owns.

        HOW THE RECORD TYPE IS TESTED, AND WHY NOT RecordTypeId. Criterion 2 reads the formula
        checkbox Disposition__c.Is_On_Market__c and requires False. Three reasons over a
        RecordTypeId criteriaItem: the criteriaItems shape is unchanged from the four other
        approval files in this repo (only the field and value are new, so nothing unproven is
        being introduced); a RecordTypeId criterion is matched by record-type LABEL, which is
        cosmetic org state and drifts silently on a rename; and Is_On_Market__c resolves to
        RecordType.DeveloperName, which is the discriminator this repo already standardises on
        in All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression and LOI__c.Is_Advance_Allowed__c.
        ⚠ A MASTER-RECORD-TYPE ROW reads FALSE on Is_On_Market__c and would therefore ENTER this
        process. That is FAIL-OPEN, and it is bounded: DispositionService stamps a record type
        explicitly on every row it creates, and DispositionApprovalService's server-side assert
        refuses an illegitimate submission before the platform ever evaluates entry criteria.
        ⚠ IF A DEPLOY EVER REJECTS A CHECKBOX CRITERION HERE, the substitute is
        <formula>AND(ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, 'Broker Selection'),
        RecordType.DeveloperName = 'Off_Market')</formula> replacing the whole <entryCriteria>
        body. Do not substitute a RecordTypeId label match.

        🔴 IT NOW CARRIES A FINAL APPROVAL ACTION, AND IT IS A SEMAPHORE, NOT A STAGE WRITE.
        The retracted sentence above said no field updates fire, on the (correct) reasoning that
        an approval FieldUpdate bypasses validation rules. That objection is answered rather than
        ignored: Set_Approval_Advance_Pending writes a FLAG. The flag re-fires DispositionTrigger,
        which enqueues DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, which writes the stage with ordinary
        Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE) - so validation rules DO evaluate.
        The Queueable maps Broker Selection to NDA for Off_Market ONLY, which is the same scoping
        criterion 2 enforces here; the two must stay in step.

        approvalPageFields DROPS Brokers_Contacted__c / Responses_Received__c /
        Submission_Deadline__c, which described a BOV round that does not happen off-market.

        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-20. THE SENTENCE THAT USED TO SIT HERE IS FALSE AND IS RETRACTED IN
        PLACE, NOT BELOW, SO IT CANNOT BE READ ON ITS OWN:

            RETRACTED: "approvalPageFields now leads with Selected_Broker__c - on this path that
            field IS the decision."

        WHY IT DIED: the off-market broker pick is now a validated Lookup(Contact),
        Disposition__c.Broker__c, and the submit gate in DispositionApprovalService reads THAT
        field. Selected_Broker__c is no longer the decision off-market; it is a DENORMALISED
        DISPLAY STRING stamped from the lookup in before-context.

        BOTH FIELDS ARE ON THE PAGE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE, NOT DUPLICATION. Broker__c leads and
        renders the Contact as a CLICKABLE NAME, which is the actual record the principal is
        approving and the only one they can open to check the person. Selected_Broker__c follows
        and carries the person and firm string inline, so the approver sees WHICH FIRM without
        navigating away from the approval page. Dropping either one costs the approver something
        real. Both need read FLS on DPEG_Disposition_View or they render blank for the approver.

        ⚠ ONE FIELD, TWO FORMATS, AND THIS PAGE SEES ONLY ONE OF THEM. Selected_Broker__c reads
        'Person - Firm' off-market and 'Firm' alone on-market. Only the off-market format ever
        reaches THIS process, because criterion 2 below restricts entry to Is_On_Market__c False.

        ⚠ RECALL ANY PENDING INSTANCES BEFORE DEPLOYING. Entry criteria change under an in-flight
        approval, and this 2026-08-20 edit changes approvalPageFields under one too. An org sweep
        on 2026-08-19 found ZERO pending ProcessInstances on Disposition__c and zero Off_Market
        rows. 🔴 THAT MEASUREMENT HAS NOW AGED PAST A DAY AND MUST BE RE RUN AT DEPLOY TIME, not
        cited. The same sweep is also what the decision to drop the old blank-text fallback in
        the submit gate rests on, so if it now returns Off_Market rows carrying hand typed
        Selected_Broker__c text, ESCALATE rather than deploying.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml and
        objects/Disposition__c/fields/Is_On_Market__c.field-meta.xml must both land FIRST.

        =====================================================================================
        2026-08-21 - THREE NEW ELEMENTS, PLUS A SECOND ACTION ON finalApprovalActions.
        =====================================================================================
        initialSubmissionActions (new) sets Disposition__c.Approval_Pending__c;
        finalApprovalActions gains Clear_Approval_Pending as a SECOND action;
        finalRejectionActions (new, this file had none) and recallActions (new) clear it.
        Set_Approval_Advance_Pending is untouched and stays FIRST. Purpose: hide the
        Submit_Broker_Selection quick action on Disposition_Record_Page while this approval is
        genuinely pending.

        🔴 THE FULL ARGUMENT, THE EVIDENCE FOR THE TWO PREVIOUSLY UNPROVEN ELEMENT SHAPES, AND
        THE MANDATORY SUBMIT-THEN-RECALL READBACK LIVE IN ONE PLACE AND ARE NOT REPEATED HERE:
        approvalProcesses/Disposition__c.Sale_Decision_Approval.approvalProcess-meta.xml,
        2026-08-21 entry. That file is deliberately deployed and behaviourally proven FIRST AND
        ALONE. Do not deploy this file until its recall test has passed, because a recallActions
        block that deploys green and never fires hides this Submit button PERMANENTLY on an
        unlocked record with no route to resubmit, and nothing logs it.

        ⚠ THIS PROCESS IS OFF-MARKET ONLY (criterion 2 above), but the flag it writes is shared
        with the other three Submit actions. That is safe ONLY because the four entry stages are
        mutually exclusive and each Dynamic Action rule already ANDs its own stage, so one flag
        is target scoped by construction. Same dependency the "ONE UPDATE SERVES ALL THREE
        APPROVALS" note in workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml records for the semaphore.

        ⚠ Approval_Pending__c AND Approval_Advance_Pending__c ARE OPPOSITES IN TIME AND ARE NOT
        INTERCHANGEABLE. Read the banner on
        objects/Disposition__c/fields/Approval_Pending__c.field-meta.xml first.

        =====================================================================================
        2026-08-26 - LABEL RENAME ONLY. Process <label> changed from "Broker Selection Approval"
        to "Broker Selection Approval (Off-Market)"; step <label> changed from "Principal Review"
        to "Principal confirms broker". All five disposition approvals previously carried the
        step label "Principal Review", so approvers saw identical names on every approval request
        and could not tell which decision they were being asked for. fullName / developer name
        (Disposition__c.Broker_Selection_Approval) and step <name> (Principal_Review_Step) are
        UNCHANGED. Zero runtime impact: DispositionApprovalService.submit calls
        Approval.process(request) with only setObjectId set, auto-routed by entryCriteria alone,
        never by name or label - confirmed by grep across force-app/main/default/classes, which
        found no setProcessDefinitionNameOrId call anywhere in the repo.
        =====================================================================================
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <allowRecall>true</allowRecall>
    <allowedSubmitters>
        <type>owner</type>
    </allowedSubmitters>
    <approvalPageFields>
        <field>Name</field>
        <field>Owner</field>
        <field>Disposition_Stage__c</field>
        <field>Broker__c</field>
        <field>Selected_Broker__c</field>
        <field>Property_Asset__c</field>
    </approvalPageFields>
    <approvalStep>
        <allowDelegate>false</allowDelegate>
        <assignedApprover>
            <approver>
                <name>nikhil.dhanani@usmandpeg.uat</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <approver>
                <name>aftab.ali.dpeg.usman@avanzasolutions.com</name>
                <type>user</type>
            </approver>
            <whenMultipleApprovers>FirstResponse</whenMultipleApprovers>
        </assignedApprover>
        <label>Principal confirms broker</label>
        <name>Principal_Review_Step</name>
    </approvalStep>
    <description>OFF-MARKET ONLY. Principal decision to confirm the directly picked broker. Entry: stage is Broker Selection AND Is On Market is false. Approval fires the Set_Approval_Advance_Pending semaphore; a Queueable then advances the stage to NDA.</description>
    <enableMobileDeviceAccess>false</enableMobileDeviceAccess>
    <entryCriteria>
        <booleanFilter>1 AND 2</booleanFilter>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Disposition__c.Disposition_Stage__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Broker Selection</value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Disposition__c.Is_On_Market__c</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>False</value>
        </criteriaItems>
    </entryCriteria>
    <finalApprovalActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Approval_Advance_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalApprovalActions>
    <finalApprovalRecordLock>false</finalApprovalRecordLock>
    <finalRejectionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </finalRejectionActions>
    <finalRejectionRecordLock>false</finalRejectionRecordLock>
    <initialSubmissionActions>
        <action>
            <name>Set_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </initialSubmissionActions>
    <label>Broker Selection Approval (Off-Market)</label>
    <processOrder>2</processOrder>
    <recallActions>
        <action>
            <name>Clear_Approval_Pending</name>
            <type>FieldUpdate</type>
        </action>
    </recallActions>
    <recordEditability>AdminOnly</recordEditability>
    <showApprovalHistory>true</showApprovalHistory>
</ApprovalProcess>
